    "degrade_reason": null,
    "globalConstraints": "- The chosen filter lives in the store's values under the id `filter` and nowhere else \u2014 never in React state, never in a URL, never in a second store.\n- The values schema entry `filter` is `{type: 'string'}` with no `default`, so `getContent()` of a store that was never filtered carries an empty values half and every snapshot file that existed at BASE loads to itself. A `default` on that entry is a finding.\n- Nothing this plan asserts pins the exact key set of `TABLES_SCHEMA`, of a todos row, or of the store's tables: two sibling runs on the same base add a cell to `todos` and a `trash` table concurrently, and the fold at publish must leave all three green. A test that lists every table or every cell of a row is a finding. `TABLES_SCHEMA` and `INVARIANTS` are not edited by this plan.\n- `#doneCount` is derived from every row of `todos` whatever the filter holds \u2014 `countTodos` and `DoneCount` are not edited by this plan.\n- No exam file bundles the page twice: at most one `stateExam` that names an `entry` per exam file, and any further check in that file is an ordinary `bun:test` block, because a second `Bun.build` in one `bun test` process fails with `Bundle failed` (measured on Bun 1.3.0; recorded on the fleet in `tests/state-exams/interaction-evidence.test.ts`'s header).\n- The static page `renderStatic` paints for the linter and the live page paint the same markup for the same state: the bar is mounted once, in `TodoList`, which both pages render.\n- The linter's own exams under `packages/tinyapp-lint/test/` read their expectations from the tree \u2014 the snapshot list, the exam list and the callback list computed from the directories and the store module, counts as floors \u2014 and carry no exact count of snapshots, exams or seeds and no frozen callback list. Two sibling runs on the same base add a callback and snapshots of their own, and a literal re-pinned here to a new number is a same-line conflict with theirs at publish; a re-pinned literal is a finding.",
